abstract: The Hakai Terrestrial Bioblitz (2018) was an intensive biodiversity survey
  of the forests, bogs, and beaches around Calvert Island, BC. Target species included
  insects, plants, lichens, birds, and mammals. Whenever possible, teams of taxonomists
  and field biologists made collections of specimens that were morphologically identified
  in the lab, photographed, and then processed for DNA barcoding, with the resulting
  sequence data added to the Barcode of Life Datasystem (BOLD). Voucher specimens
  from these collections were accessioned at the Royal BC Museum. Many additional
  observations were recorded on iNaturalist. This survey resulted in the identification
  of new species and expanded the known range of many others.
